      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p41-q55-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Both sides equal ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{(n-1)!\\,n!\\,(n+1)!}{(k-1)!\\,k!\\,(k+1)!\\,(n-k-1)!\\,(n-k)!\\,(n-k+1)!}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p41-q55-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Expand each combination into factorials and rearrange the common factors.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Expanding the left-hand side into factorials gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n-1}{k-1}\\binom{n}{k+1}\\binom{n+1}{k}&=\\frac{(n-1)!}{(k-1)!(n-k)!}\\frac{n!}{(k+1)!(n-k-1)!}\\frac{(n+1)!}{k!(n-k+1)!}\\\\\\binom{n-1}{k-1}\\binom{n}{k+1}\\binom{n+1}{k}&=\\frac{(n-1)!\\,n!\\,(n+1)!}{(k-1)!\\,k!\\,(k+1)!\\,(n-k-1)!\\,(n-k)!\\,(n-k+1)!}.\\end{align*}$$\nExpanding the right-hand side gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{n-1}{k}\\binom{n}{k-1}\\binom{n+1}{k+1}&=\\frac{(n-1)!}{k!(n-k-1)!}\\frac{n!}{(k-1)!(n-k+1)!}\\frac{(n+1)!}{(k+1)!(n-k)!}\\\\\\binom{n-1}{k}\\binom{n}{k-1}\\binom{n+1}{k+1}&=\\frac{(n-1)!\\,n!\\,(n+1)!}{(k-1)!\\,k!\\,(k+1)!\\,(n-k-1)!\\,(n-k)!\\,(n-k+1)!}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe products are equal, proving the identity.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
